WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.330
Snip three shoots from one parent
plant, and root each one in its own pot.

2
00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:08.660
Every cutting carries
exactly the same DNA.

3
00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:11.330
Not similar: identical.

4
00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:14.410
Later, they stand at
three different heights.

5
00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:19.030
So if they share every gene, why don't
they all grow to the same height?

6
00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:22.970
In this mission, you'll pull
apart two words that sound alike:

7
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:27.310
genotype, the alleles an
organism has, and phenotype,

8
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.300
its observable traits.

9
00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:32.240
Then you'll put those two
words to work on a new case,

10
00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:34.140
in a different living thing.

11
00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:39.170
Your mission: explain why cuttings with
identical genes still grow to different

12
00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:39.890
heights.
